# ==========================================================
# Cloudflare redirect rules (Cloudflare Pages / wrangler)
# ==========================================================
# Format: <from>  <to>  [status]
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# These mirror the .htaccess rules (which GitHub Pages does not
# execute) and the Redirect Rules documented in cloudflare/README.md.
#
# ⚠️ IMPORTANT — do NOT add `/foo` → `/foo.html` rules here.
# Cloudflare Pages already serves extensionless URLs natively and
# 308-redirects `/foo.html` → `/foo`, so such a rule creates an
# infinite redirect loop. GitHub Pages cannot serve extensionless
# URLs at all; that behaviour is provided by a Cloudflare Redirect
# Rule (Path A, step A4), not by this file.
# ============================================================

# --- Legacy brand domain -> canonical host (production only) ---------
# Cloudflare Pages applies absolute-URL (domain-level) rules at the
# edge in production; `wrangler pages dev` skips them by design.
https://legacylaunchpad.co.za/*        https://www.neonlegacies.co.za/:splat   301
https://www.legacylaunchpad.co.za/*    https://www.neonlegacies.co.za/:splat   301

# --- Apex -> www (single canonical origin, avoids duplicate content) --
https://neonlegacies.co.za/*           https://www.neonlegacies.co.za/:splat   301

# --- Safety net: unknown paths must 404, never fall back to index -----
# `404.html` in the repository root is served by both Cloudflare Pages
# and GitHub Pages for unmatched paths, so no catch-all rule is needed
# here (and a catch-all would break the 404 status code).

